The documentation (docs/, the text of the lessons in lessons/ and the
executed notebooks in lessons/notebooks/) is licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ — reuse with attribution to
Jochen Köhler, JCSS CodeCal 2.0, https://github.com/jochenkohler/JCSS_CodeCal_2_0.

The probabilistic model (codecal/ahg2021.py) is the input agreed by the
CEN/TC 250/SC 10 Ad-hoc Group "Reliability Background of the Eurocodes"
(2021), published in the JRC Technical Report "Reliability background of
the Eurocodes" (2024, CC BY 4.0, doi:10.2760/9482837). The calibration
study it reproduces is the work of Jochen Köhler, Ramon Hingorani and
John Dalsgaard Sørensen.
